    {t:"The &ldquo;News Chain&rdquo; game", b:"Imagine you tell a secret to two friends, each of them tells two new people the next day, and so on. Draw a &ldquo;tree&rdquo; on paper and count how many people learn the secret on the first, second, third, fourth, and fifth day. Write these numbers as powers of two and check that on the fifth day it's 2^5 = 32 people."},
    {t:"Units of length and powers of ten", b:"Take a ruler and find the millimeters, centimeters, and decimeters on it. Write down how many millimeters there are in 1 cm, in 1 dm, and in 1 m, using powers of 10 (for example, in 1 m there are 1,000 mm = 10^3 mm). What pattern do you notice between the exponent and the number of zeros?"}
