CONTENT_EN.perc.steps = [
  {title:"What a percent is", body:
    "<p>A percent is one hundredth: 1% = {1|100} = 0.01. So 50% = 0.5 = {1|2}; 25% = {1|4}; 10% = 0.1.</p><div class='figure'>__SVG_PERC_GRID__</div><p>The square is split into 100 cells — each cell is 1%. 2 columns (20 cells) are shaded, plus 5 more cells: 25 cells in total, that is, 25% = {25|100} = {1|4} = 0.25.</p>"},
  {title:"Three basic problems", body:
    "<h3>Three basic problems</h3><ul><li><b>Find p% of a number.</b> Number · p : 100. For example, 15% of 240: 240 · 0.15 = 36.</li><li><b>What percent one number is of another.</b> (part : whole) · 100%. For example, 18 of 72: 18 : 72 = 0.25, that is, 25%.</li><li><b>Find a number from its part.</b> Part : p · 100. If 20% of a number equals 14, then 1% equals 0.7, and the whole number is 70.</li></ul>",
    exIdx:[0,1]},
  {title:"How to find a percent of a number: find 1% first", body:
    "<div class='figure'>__SVG_PERC_OF_ANIM__</div><p>First we find 1% (number : 100), then multiply it by the number of percent we need.</p>",
    exIdx:[6,8]},
  {title:"Discounts and markups", body:
    "<h3>Discounts and markups</h3><p>If the price rises by 15%, the new price equals the old one multiplied by 1.15. If the price falls by 30%, the new price equals the old one multiplied by 0.7.</p>",
    exIdx:[2,4]},
  {title:"Percents one after another (two operations in a row)", body:
    "<h3>Percents one after another (two operations in a row)</h3><p>If the price was first raised by 10% and then lowered by 20%, you can't simply subtract 20% − 10% = 10%. Each next percent is figured from the <b>already changed</b> price: 100 → 100 · 1.1 = 110 → 110 · 0.8 = 88. The total change isn't 10%, but 12% (with a minus sign).</p><div class='figure'>__SVG_PERC_STEPS__</div><p>The diagram shows: the price of 100 ₽ became 110 ₽ after +10%, and after −20% of <b>110 ₽</b> it became 88 ₽. That's 12 ₽ below the original, that is, −12%, not −10%.</p>",
    exIdx:[3]},
  {title:"Common mistake: a discount and a markup don't cancel out", body:
    "<div class='warn'><span class='hand'>Common mistake</span>A 20% discount followed by a 20% markup doesn't bring the price back to what it was: 100 → 80 → 96. Each time, the percent is figured from the <b>new</b> price, not the original one.</div><div class='figure'>__SVG_PERC5_DISCOUNT_MARKUP__</div>",
    exIdx:[7]},
  {title:"A quick trick for percents", body:
    "<div class='note'><span class='hand'>Quick trick</span>10% of a number — move the decimal point one place to the left. 5% is half of 10%. 1% — move the decimal point two places. 12.5% is {1|8}, that is, divide the number by 8.</div>",
    exIdx:[5]}
];

